WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.176
Every catalog item runs the same loop:
a typed request against a named target,

2
00:00:05.176 --> 00:00:09.651
the approval its control needs,
execution under a narrow identity,

3
00:00:09.651 --> 00:00:13.800
and a record that closes only
when a check confirms the change.

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.941
Every identity change is one
of five verbs: add, move,

5
00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:22.575
change, delete or reset, and
each has its own closing check.

6
00:00:22.575 --> 00:00:25.100
The one that fails audits is the leaver.

7
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:29.507
Disabling the account isn't enough;
sessions, connected applications

8
00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:33.762
and everything the person owned all
have to be handled and recorded.

9
00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:37.283
Apps without automatic
provisioning become manual tasks,

10
00:00:37.283 --> 00:00:40.588
with no automatic check that
the account is really gone.

11
00:00:40.588 --> 00:00:43.990
Telephony has its own
catalog, with real stakes.
